+
+    NuRec patch. A package that cannot be linked as one directory (e.g. because
+    it contains shared libraries) gets its files linked one by one into a real
+    venv directory. Python looks for bytecode in `__pycache__` next to the `.py`
+    it imports, i.e. inside that venv directory. When every `.py` of a venv
+    directory comes from the same runfiles directory, the `__pycache__` next to
+    them is linked there, as one directory link. When they come from several
+    (merged prefix groups, and the site-packages root where every wheel's
+    top-level modules land), a wheel's `__pycache__` may hold bytecode for a
+    module name whose `.py` was selected from another wheel, and Python would
+    run that bytecode: each selected `.py` gets the pyc files of its own
+    `__pycache__` linked one by one instead. Existing entries of `keep_map` win.
+    A directory link needs nothing: it exposes the runfiles `__pycache__` as is.
